# Pinned hashes for the root QA tree, which is maintained OUTSIDE this repository.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, the same commit produced different `make check` scopes and
# different `make dist` tarballs depending on what happened to be lying in the working
# directory. The tree's identity has to be a fact about the commit, and this is that fact.
#
# What it covers: EVERY file under test/, not a chosen subset. An earlier version pinned only
# test/{functional,fuzz,util,sanitizer_suppressions} -- 338 of 379 files -- which left
# test/lint/** and test/get_previous_releases.py free to drift while the pin still verified.
# A partial pin is a partial identity, and it reads like a whole one.
#
# Excluded, deliberately and by rule rather than by list: __pycache__ and *.pyc/*.pyo, because
# generated caches are not part of anyone's QA identity; test/cache/, written by test runs;
# test/config.ini, generated by configure; and test/config.ini.in, which is TRACKED IN GIT --
# its identity is the commit's own, not this external tree's.
#
# What it does NOT do: distribute the tree. `make dist` never packages these paths, and the
# published repository does not carry test/ at all -- see the note in Makefile.am. This file
# pins what a development checkout must be holding for its QA results to mean anything, and
# `make check-qa-tree` is what verifies it.
#
# It lives at the top level, NOT under test/, precisely because test/ is not published. The
# pin is a statement the repository makes ABOUT an external tree; it is not part of that tree.
#
# Regenerate deliberately, never as a side effect of a QA run, and say why in the commit.
